  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is positive (0.00–0.67) and model shows over-optimism (e.g., overshoots true price by >5% in early days).",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes: if last 3–5 days show upward momentum, apply a 10–15% lagged correction to prevent over-forecasting.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is >10% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 1–2% per day until convergence.",
    "When sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25), reduce forecast by 2–3% relative to prior 30d average to avoid underestimating downside risk.",
    "For horizon >14 days, apply a 1–2% downward bias to account for delayed market reaction and policy-induced volatility."
  ]
}
